'' A PROPERTY SETTER'S VALUE THROUGH A CONVERSION CONSTRUCTOR, as a call's argument: 'o.P = 5' over
'' 'byref v as V' and 'constructor V( byval n as long )', byval and indexed too. tiko scored no setter
'' and dropped the statement (TKO0994) -- CDispInvoke's 'pDisp.Put( "Pattern" ) = ".is"'. Expected
'' output is fbc-modern's, temporaries destroyed after each call.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/setter-ctor-conv.bas -o tests/codegen/setterctorconv.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/setterctorconv.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P 5 n5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: sctor hey
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: P 3 hey
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Q 1 6 n6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: ctor 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Put id 2 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: sctor abc
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Put name 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: dtor 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: end
